Chapter: EdgeMeshPlanes

  cites Engine chapter EdgeMesh
  cites Mesh chapter EdgeMeshFederate
  cites CodexMagic chapter GameRegistry

 `EdgeMeshGameServers.md` phase 3, stage 5: the games quire decides what a game
 IS, and phase 3 stage 1 keys a queue lane by a name the caller supplies. The
 bridge is here, above both, and cites `GameRegistry` alone because game
 identity is all the bridge needs (L-SUBSET).

 THE LANE KEY CARRIES THE GAME ID, not the display name alone. Two registered
 games are permitted to share a display name, and a lane keyed by name alone
 would fuse the two and hand back exactly the cross-game pairing stage 1 exists
 to refuse.

 AN UNKNOWN ID IS REFUSED RATHER THAN TRANSLATED. `find-game` answers a
 fabricated `RegisteredGame` for an id nobody registered, carrying
 `game-id = -1` and the display name "Unknown" (`GameRegistry.codex:115`), so a
 bridge that translated the name would put every unknown id into one lane named
 "Unknown" and pair players from different games inside the lane. The test is
 `game-id`, and never the name: a registered game is permitted to be called
 "Unknown".

Section: Naming A Lane

  plane-lane : RegisteredGame -> Text
  plane-lane (g) = (g.name) & "#" & show (g.game-id)

Section: Admitting A Player

  PlaneAdmit =
    | Admitted (FedQueue) (Text)
    | AdmitRefused (Text)

  plane-admit : GameRegistryState, FedQueue, Integer, QueuedPlayer -> PlaneAdmit
  plane-admit (reg) (q) (game-id) (p) =
    let g = find-game reg game-id
    in if (g.game-id) < 0 then AdmitRefused ("no game registered with id " & show game-id)
    else if (g.active) == False then AdmitRefused ((g.name) & " is registered and not active")
    else Admitted (fed-enqueue q (plane-lane g) p) (plane-lane g)

  plane-queue : PlaneAdmit, FedQueue -> FedQueue
  plane-queue (a) (fallback) =
    when a
      is Admitted (q) (lane) -> q
      is AdmitRefused (why) -> fallback

Section: Reporting

  plane-admit-label : PlaneAdmit -> Text
  plane-admit-label (a) =
    when a
      is Admitted (q) (lane) -> "admitted to lane " & lane
      is AdmitRefused (why) -> "refused: " & why
